.TH rmdir "" "Command"
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrmdir [\-f] \fIdirectory ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
rmdir -- remove directory
Usage:	rmdir [ -f ] directory ...
Option:	-f	Force override of empty and name checks for superuser
.HE
.B rmdir
removes each named
.IR directory .
A directory must be empty before it can be removed: it may contain no entries
other than
.B .
and
.BR .. .
.IP \fB\-f\fR
Force the removal.
For the superuser, this overrides the checks that the
.I directory
is empty and is not
.B .
or
.BR .. .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR rm ,
.B unlink()
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B rmdir
returns a nonzero exit status if any
.I directory
could not be removed, typically because it is not empty, does not exist, or the
caller lacks permission.
.SH NOTES
.B rmdir
will not remove a directory that is the working directory of any process.
